{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787314021684114881,"compiled_state":{"alias":"material-sciophilic-echidna","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"d68b471df1debbb1d4c5d7913a6701f95b2ba11e38cbf84289d088321c910b20","event_uuid":"c3648e73-2557-426d-9ece-46afb0462638","position":{"commit_sha":"b7af132b8ad413d253a1b12f86ab95e23a99f974","position":"1787312098916508001-c3648e73-2557-426d-9ece-46afb0462638"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7980cf3458f050a4cbd3cd22a3a5d516075255d164ddccdf352c1d4921f0608c","event_uuid":"f83f21ed-99cf-4566-ae1e-39e3872d19ef","position":{"commit_sha":"85943bc6786e6fca2bae90f9b6e00193819a3eca","position":"1787312118466735001-f83f21ed-99cf-4566-ae1e-39e3872d19ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787312098916508001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f83f21ed-99cf-4566-ae1e-39e3872d19ef","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"84c7-486f-9a13-4c3f"}],"description":"## Observation\nAfter bug 84c7 removed the four ghost rows, **all 9 remaining `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` rows\ndeclare an empty prefix**. `_rebar_env: (0, \"REBAR_\")` was the only row that ever used the\nsecond tuple element, and its helper was drained out of the tree by the RP-04 cutover\n(`d361eb28e4`).\n\nThe prefix is still applied at `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` `_scan_call`\n(`reads.setdefault(prefix + lit, ...)`) and at `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`\n`_helper_access` (`return self._resolved_env(node, prefix + lit)`).\n\n## Why it matters\nThe feature now has **zero production users and zero live end-to-end coverage**. It was\nalso mis-covered before: `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` asserted\n`REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE in reads` under the comment \"a `_rebar_env(\\\"SUFFIX\\\")`\nreconciler read resolved with the REBAR_ prefix\", but that variable has been captured by a\nplain inline `os.environ.get(\"REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE\", \"0\")` at\n`_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:406` since the shim was drained\n— so the assertion passed for a different reason than it claimed. 84c7 corrected that\ncomment but did not add real prefix coverage.\n\nNote the 84c7 fix did add *some* prefix coverage in the ownership gate's held-out fixture\n(`test_known_env_helper_call_resolves_and_fires` now asserts `prefix + \"SOME_KNOB\"`),\nbut with every live prefix empty that assertion is currently vacuous.\n\n## Options\n- **Add a synthetic-tree test** that registers a prefixed row and asserts both scanners\n  apply it. Cheap, keeps the feature honest.\n- **Remove the prefix field** if nothing is expected to need it again, simplifying both\n  tables to a bare int. This is a behaviour-narrowing change and needs its own review.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Either prefixed resolution has a test that fails when the prefix is dropped, or the\n      field is removed from both consumers.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` stay green.\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` is unchanged by the work (no live row uses a prefix).\n\n## Provenance\nObserved while fixing bug 84c7 (surprised-convincing-gopher); recorded rather than repaired\nthere, because adding coverage for an unused feature is outside the scope of restoring the\ntable->tree invariant.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3a57-82b0-74bb-44e8","ticket_type":"task","title":"KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS prefix field has no live user and no live coverage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c3648e73-2557-426d-9ece-46afb0462638","f83f21ed-99cf-4566-ae1e-39e3872d19ef"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787314021684114881,"uuid":"5c5566d3-bb56-4a56-8589-e294cd0b318b"}